# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps secrets and host-built binaries
# out of the image. apps/service/Dockerfile copies the whole repo into a throwaway stage to
# collect workspace manifests, so anything not excluded here would be sent to the daemon.
#
# Do not exclude package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, or pnpm-workspace.yaml: the manifest stage
# needs every one of them to resolve the workspace graph.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Host-built output. The image installs and runs from source; a macOS-built dist would be
# both useless and, for native dependencies, wrong.
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
*.tgz

# Never bake credentials into a layer. .env is gitignored, which does not stop Docker.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor/agent scratch that has no business in a build context.
.context
.DS_Store
